    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "GEO is the work of optimizing your content and brand so that generative AI engines — ChatGPT, Google's AI Overviews, Perplexity, Gemini — cite you when they answer a buyer's question. You will also see it called AI search optimization or answer engine optimization. The simplest way to think about it: SEO is a fight for a ranking, GEO is a fight for a mention inside the answer the AI writes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is GEO different from SEO?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It grows out of SEO but it is not the same job. Strong, well-organised content helps with both, true, but GEO adds its own layer on top: passage-level structure an engine can lift cleanly, entity and Q&A schema, and brand mentions across the places these models learn to trust. So we run GEO on top of solid SEO, never instead of it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which AI engines do you optimize for?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Whichever ones your buyers are actually using — in practice that means Google's AI Overviews and AI Mode, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini. We run your priority prompts through each, see who is getting cited today, and put the effort where your audience and the opportunity line up."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you guarantee my brand gets cited?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No, and the same caveat applies as with a Google ranking — the engine makes the call, not us. What we can genuinely do is move the odds: build the structure, schema, and brand signals these engines reward, then track your citations over time so you can watch the trend rather than take it on faith."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you measure GEO results?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We run your target prompts across each engine on a regular schedule and record how often — and how prominently — your brand turns up. That gives you a month-over-month trend per engine instead of a single snapshot, so you can actually see whether the work is landing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it too early to invest in GEO?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Honestly, early is the whole point. AI answers already show up on a large share of searches and more buyers start with ChatGPT every month, yet hardly any local competitors are optimising for it. Earning these engines' trust now is far cheaper than trying to claw your way in once everyone else has noticed."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
